Generic single-database configuration.

First, ensure the db you're connecting to is up. To run Alembic commands, first `cd app/`.

1. make sure your db is up to date (upgrade version): `alembic upgrade head`
2. downgrade version: `alembic downgrade head-1` (etc)
3. create a new revision: `alembic revision -m "description" --autogenerate`
   1. This autogenerates the observed changes but *cannot* capture everything, so verify that the autogenerated file is correct and test it by upgrading the version.

Note: when bootstrapping the app for the first time, you should only need to run `alembic upgrade head`. You can confirm it works by noting the correct tables having been populated in your database.
